---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'July 25, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Discord Bot Terms and Privacy - OpenClaw"
  description="Terms of Service and Privacy Policy for the Discord bots operated by OpenClaw."
  canonicalUrl="https://openclaw.ai/bot-terms"
>
  <div class="stars"></div>
  <div class="nebula"></div>

  <main class="container">
    <header class="header">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to home</a>
      <p class="eyebrow">OpenClaw Discord Bots</p>
      <h1 class="title">Terms of Service &amp; Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        Simple version: these bots are operated by the OpenClaw project for its own community and
        team. They read messages in the channels they are invited to, send that text to AI model
        providers to produce a reply, and store the conversation on servers we control. We do not
        sell your data or show ads.
      </p>
      <p class="effective">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <section class="policy-card oc-card" id="terms">
      <h2>Terms of Service</h2>

      <h3>Who we are and what this covers</h3>
      <p>
        These terms cover the Discord applications operated by the OpenClaw project, including
        <strong>Roboclaw</strong>, <strong>Molty</strong>, <strong>ClawSweeper</strong>,
        <strong>Mantis</strong>, and <strong>Tideclaw</strong> (each, a &ldquo;bot&rdquo;). The bots
        are built on the open-source OpenClaw project and are run by the project maintainers. By
        using a bot, or by participating in a channel where one is present, you agree to these
        terms.
      </p>

      <h3>What the service does</h3>
      <p>
        Each bot is an AI assistant. It reads messages addressed to it, and in some channels the
        surrounding conversation, and replies using third-party AI models. Replies are generated by
        software and may be wrong, incomplete, or out of date. Do not rely on a bot for legal,
        financial, medical, or safety-critical decisions, and verify anything that matters.
      </p>

      <h3>Acceptable use</h3>
      <p>You agree not to use a bot to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>break Discord&rsquo;s Terms of Service or Community Guidelines, or any applicable law;</li>
        <li>harass, threaten, defame, or impersonate anyone;</li>
        <li>generate or distribute malware, spam, or content that sexualises minors;</li>
        <li>attempt to extract credentials, secrets, or other users&rsquo; private data; or</li>
        <li>deliberately disrupt the service, for example by automated flooding.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may rate-limit, ignore, remove, or block any user, channel, or server at our discretion,
        with or without notice.
      </p>

      <h3>Availability and changes</h3>
      <p>
        The bots are provided free of charge, as-is and as-available, with no warranty of any kind.
        We may change, suspend, or discontinue any bot at any time, and we do not guarantee uptime,
        response quality, or retention of any conversation. To the fullest extent permitted by law,
        the OpenClaw project and its maintainers are not liable for any damages arising from use of
        the bots.
      </p>

      <h3>Your content</h3>
      <p>
        You keep any rights you have in what you write. You grant us permission to process your
        messages as described in the Privacy Policy below, for the purpose of operating the service.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes to these terms</h3>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The effective date above changes when we do. Continued use after
        an update means you accept the revised terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-card oc-card" id="privacy">
      <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>

      <h3>What we process</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Message content</strong> in channels and threads where a bot is present and
          permitted to read, and in direct messages you send to a bot. In most channels a bot only
          receives messages that mention it; where a server operator has enabled it, a bot may
          receive other messages in that channel as context.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Identifiers and metadata</strong>: Discord user, channel, server, and message IDs,
          display names, timestamps, and the roles relevant to access control.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Attachments and links</strong> you send to a bot, when the bot needs them to
          answer.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not request or store your Discord password, email, or payment details.</p>

      <h3>Why we process it</h3>
      <p>
        To generate replies, to maintain conversation context, to operate access controls and abuse
        protection, and to diagnose faults. We do not use your messages to train our own models, we
        do not sell or rent your data, and we do not run advertising or third-party analytics inside
        the bots.
      </p>

      <h3>Who else sees it</h3>
      <p>
        To produce a reply, message text and relevant context are sent to third-party AI model
        providers, which currently include OpenAI and Anthropic. Their handling is governed by their
        own terms and privacy policies. Server operators and maintainers with administrative access
        to the machine running a bot can read stored conversations for that bot.
      </p>

      <h3>Where it is stored</h3>
      <p>
        Conversations are stored on servers controlled by the project maintainers, currently hosted
        with Hetzner in the United States and Germany, and on maintainer-operated machines. There is
        no central OpenClaw cloud that aggregates bot conversations across unrelated servers.
      </p>

      <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
      <p>
        Conversation history is retained so a bot can maintain context, and is kept until it is no
        longer needed for operating the service or until deletion is requested. Diagnostic logs are
        kept for a shorter period. We may retain records where we are legally required to.
      </p>

      <h3>Your choices</h3>
      <p>
        You can stop sharing data with a bot by not addressing it and by leaving or muting channels
        where it is present. You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of the data we
        hold about you, and depending on where you live you may have additional rights under laws
        such as the GDPR. Requests that would require deleting other people&rsquo;s messages, or
        that conflict with a legal obligation, may be limited in scope.
      </p>

      <h3>Children</h3>
      <p>
        The bots are not directed at children. You must meet Discord&rsquo;s minimum age
        requirement for your country to use them.
      </p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>
        For privacy requests, security reports, or questions about these terms, contact
        <a href="mailto:service@openclaw.org">service@openclaw.org</a>, or open an issue at
        <a href="https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw">github.com/openclaw/openclaw</a>. Security
        issues should follow the disclosure process in that repository&rsquo;s
        <code>SECURITY.md</code>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <SiteFooter />
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .container {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px var(--oc-space-6) 96px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--oc-text-secondary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--oc-accent-primary);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 24px 0 4px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--oc-text-secondary);
  }

  .title {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
  }

  .subtitle {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: var(--oc-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .effective {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--oc-text-secondary);
  }

  .policy-card {
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding: 28px 26px;
    border-radius: var(--oc-radius-surface);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .policy-card h3 {
    margin: 26px 0 8px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .policy-card p,
  .policy-card li {
    color: var(--oc-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .policy-card ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: var(--oc-accent-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .policy-card a:hover {
    color: var(--oc-accent-secondary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .container {
      padding: 28px var(--oc-space-4) 56px;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 22px 18px;
      border-radius: var(--oc-radius-surface);
    }

    .subtitle {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
